coder › Implemented and verified. Summary of what I did:

**`src/ini.ts`** — Replaced the stub with the full `parseIni` implementation following the spec:
- Split on `/\r?\n/`, tracking a 1-based line number.
- Blank lines and `;`/`#` comments (after trim) ignored.
- Section headers matched against `/^\[(.*)\]$/`; captured group trimmed (empty → `''`); a bracket-leading line that doesn't match throws.
- Key/value split at the first `=` with both parts trimmed; a value that both starts and ends with `"` has exactly those two outer quotes stripped, keeping the interior verbatim.
- Anything else throws `SyntaxError("Invalid INI line at line N")`.
- Current section starts as `''`; sections created lazily via `result[currentSection] ??= {}` so later keys override.

**`src/ini.test.ts`** — Added tests for all the listed behaviors (keys before a header under `''`, multiple sections, whitespace trimming, blank lines, `;`/`#` comments incl. after leading whitespace, quoted values preserving spaces/`;`, first-`=` split, override, and the SyntaxError message with verified 1-based line 3), plus two spec-implied extras: empty section name `[]`, and malformed headers throwing.

